{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score","id":1245867,"title":"Maximum Achievable Attribute Score?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-14T07:05:34-07:00","id":1245867,"title":"Maximum Achievable Attribute Score?","content":"Hello. I was wondering what the maximum rating in an Attribute a character can get is with supernatural powers and a power stat of 10, and which splat can do it. I am referring to playable splats here, so not things like Rank 6+ spirits. For the purposes of this, I am referring to powers that last at least a full turn as opposed to for a single roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T09:38:19-07:00","id":1245921,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there's probably something better, but off the top of my head an Uratha can gut up to 19 Strength for their Gauru form duration:<br /> <br /> Primal Urge 10, Strength 10, Purity 5, the Purity Strength Facet, Gauru Form, Favored Form (Gauru, +1 Strength) 2+, gets you there.<br /> <br /> It feels like most splats hit the 15-16 range since they don't have something like Gauru to give them a boost on top of the basic Strength 10 + 5 from powers, plus something else thing (esp, things that give you a +1 to your Attribute max for one Attribute).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:05:35-07:00","id":1245971,"title":"","content":"Do you mean actual Attribute dots or would bonuses to all rolls involving that Attribute suffice?<br /> <br /> Edit: I ask because it's the difference between vampires having 15 or 55 in a Physical Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-14-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T14:13:30-07:00","id":1246049,"title":"","content":"Rahu werewolves can temporarily reach arbitrarily high levels of Strength via Crimson Spasm, if you're lucky enough to just keep rolling those 10s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T14:15:38-07:00","id":1246050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1246049#post1246049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rahu werewolves can temporarily reach arbitrarily high levels of Strength via Crimson Spasm, if you're lucky enough to just keep rolling those 10s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concerning the explosion possibility, I feel like the old rule of thumb of (3 Dice=1 Success) will probably help to keep dice-variable attribute boosts useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T18:03:12-07:00","id":1246136,"title":"","content":"I forgot about Crimson Spasm... but even with just taking an average, a Primal Urge 10 character could be looking at +8 or 9 from that, on top of the 19 I already posted. That's pretty nasty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T19:17:11-07:00","id":1246153,"title":"","content":"Mages with three dots in Life (Physical Attributes) or Mind (Mental and Social Attributes) can use Perfecting spells plus an extra reach to add Spell Potency dots to an attribute and increase it above the normal attribute maximum. This can lead to very high values because of the way spellcasting works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T19:39:49-07:00","id":1246158,"title":"","content":"Creating a number for mages would probably require setting a bar for the odds of success that are acceptable, since that's going to directly impact how much oomph you can put into the spell. A mage can push themselves into a chance die for a bigger bonus, but has significant risk for doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:36:08-07:00","id":1246165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1246136#post1246136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot about Crimson Spasm... but even with just taking an average, a Primal Urge 10 character could be looking at +8 or 9 from that, on top of the 19 I already posted. That's pretty nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget about Embodiment of the Firstborn, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T20:38:14-07:00","id":1246167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1246153#post1246153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages with three dots in Life (Physical Attributes) or Mind (Mental and Social Attributes) can use Perfecting spells plus an extra reach to add Spell Potency dots to an attribute and increase it above the normal attribute maximum. This can lead to very high values because of the way spellcasting works.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can also mesh well with some of the other bonuses, since it doesn't have to target the mage casting the spell.<br /> <br /> Probably including itself, unless I am misremembering something, having a bunch of Mages team up to boost a guy into Stat Godhood seems doable.<br /> <br /> Clarifying edit, as in you could have one spell for each stat, only the highest + would actually take effect for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 08-14-2018, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T02:59:49-07:00","id":1246233,"title":"","content":"Assuming a maxed mage casting Honing the Form or Augment Mind from a Grimoire. No teamwork because that opens up to a literally infinite dice pool in theory.<br /> <br /> 4 Persona + 5*3 Sacraments = 19 bonus dice from Yantras<br /> 10 Gnosis + 5 Life/Mind + 19 Yantra + 5 Ritual Intervals + 3 Willpower - 20*2 spellfactor steps = 2 dice<br /> 5 base + 20 steps = 25 Potency<br /> 3 Reach (Rote) - 2 Reach for exceeding trait maximums - 1 Reach for switch primary spell factor (Honing the Form only, oversight?) = 0 free Reach left, meaning no Paradox<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: 2 with Rote Action (Success 75.99% of the time)<br /> Casting Time: 6 minutes<br /> Cost: 1 Mana for exceeding trait maximums<br /> Duration: 1 turn (could be 1 scene for an extra Reach)<br /> Effect: Add 25 dots to an Attribute<br /> <br /> A mage with 10 base dots could reach 35 in an Attribute this way, but as mentioned they can also cast it on someone else, like that werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 08-15-2018, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T17:08:12-07:00","id":1246473,"title":"","content":"A Beast Incarnate can get incredibly strong. At Lair 10 they can have 10 base strength, +10 from taking the Titanic Onslaught ability, +11 from spending satiety on Skin Deep. And then on top of that 31 they can get an automatic 10 successes from Cyclopean Strength, giving them the effective equivalent of ~60 strength. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, the same Beast in Horror form in their Lair could put all their bonus points into Power for a bonus of 20 instead of Titanic Onslaught's 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T02:39:07-07:00","id":1247318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1245971#post1245971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean actual Attribute dots or would bonuses to all rolls involving that Attribute suffice?<br /> <br /> Edit: I ask because it's the difference between vampires having 15 or 55 in a Physical Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the somewhat late response, Bonuses to rolls would suffice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T04:48:39-07:00","id":1247347,"title":"","content":"Physical Attributes for vampires:<br /> 10 base + 5 Vigor/Resilience/Praestantia + 10 Frenzy + 15*2 Physical Intensity = 55<br /> You can gain an additional +10 to certain Strength rolls through Riding the Wave Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T08:33:04-07:00","id":1247392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1247347#post1247347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physical Attributes for vampires:<br /> 10 base + 5 Vigor/Resilience/Praestantia + 10 Frenzy + 15*2 Physical Intensity = 55<br /> You can gain an additional +10 to certain Strength rolls through Riding the Wave Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>And with buffs from the previously optimized mage, we're at 80.<br /> (assuming a Creative Thaum Death spell that functions as Honing the Form)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:00:58-07:00","id":1249555,"title":"","content":"Might be a bit late, but I was just rereading Mortal Remains and remembered a neat trick we could probably pull for MAXIMUM OPTIMIZATION!<br /> <br /> The Knights of Saint Adrian have an Endowment where they can copy the Strength or Dexterity of the monster they are fighting to use later. So having a Knight fight that 80 Strength Vamp (if he somehow survives) would be able to kick himself up to 80 Strength, as the Endowment specifically counts temporary dots.<br /> <br /> Since these dots are all provided by the endowment and not magic, the mage from earlier can now buff this dude, sending him to 105 and breaking into tipple digits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:21:45-07:00","id":1249562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1249555#post1249555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Knights of Saint Adrian have an Endowment where they can copy the Strength or Dexterity of the monster they are fighting to use later. So having a Knight fight that 80 Strength Vamp (if he somehow survives) would be able to kick himself up to 80 Strength, as the Endowment specifically counts temporary dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even setting aside the usual problems of treating Dread Powers and other supernatural abilities as interchangeable, Physical Intensity is bonus dice, not bonus dots \u2014 it lasts a single turn and explicitly doesn't add to derived Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:45:45-07:00","id":1249564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1249562#post1249562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even setting aside the usual problems of treating Dread Powers and other supernatural abilities as interchangeable, Physical Intensity is bonus dice, not bonus dots \u2014 it lasts a single turn and explicitly doesn't add to derived Traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its really the only way to keep Endowments that focus on &quot;Dread Powers&quot; relevant. If you are throwing them against the Splat books, the extra kick couldn't hurt.<br /> <br /> Right! I just looked at the total instead of the actual way he got it &gt;_&gt;. It would still be a solid plan to take one of the other actual dot examples, but you wouldn't get nearly as high as I said you would.<br /> <br /> 19 Strength Wolf from Heavy's post, +25 from the mage, total 44.<br /> Copy the 44, add another Mage boost, and we get 69.<br /> <br /> Respectable but loses out to the Vampire's dice bonus.<br /> <br /> *Edit*<br /> <br /> I don't have the Beast book, but if the 31 listed in Helm's post is actual dots, the same tactic would get us 31+50 or 81, slightly beating the Vampire XV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18090,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","user":"Ruger","date":". 08-28-2018, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T12:47:13-07:00","id":1250033,"title":"","content":"Prometheans need some love here, even if not as impressive as a Vampire.<br /> Titan with all Corporeum and Vitality Alembics. Base: Attributes at 10, Skills at 5. Defense 15. Iniative 20. Speed 25. Health 16 (Size + Sta + Giant merit). Perception 20<br /> Vitality bonuses +10 Strength from Persistent Unconquered (+unarmed lethal, + 1 Demolisher, +Ability to cause an Earthquake with a span of 1000 yards), +10 Resolve from Persistent Unbowed (+ Steadfast, + Recovering Willpower, Defense against Mind Powers), +10 Stamina from Persistent Unbroken (+Willpower bonuses doubled for Stamina-resistance rolls, ignore physical tilts, literally immortality for a scene/until goal finished), +10 Str for breaking free of Restraints/Grapples from Persistent Unfettered (+3 Demolisher or +2 to rolls to break free).<br /> Charites -&gt; +1 Dext, All Athl-rolls exceptionally suceed at 3. All dext rolls rote + 9 again.<br /> Zephyrus-&gt; +Azoth to Wits+Composure rolls to avoid surprise, double speed, +Azoth to Initiative, +3 to Defense.<br /> Hygeius -&gt; Bonuses where Wound Penalties would apply for mortals, immunity to physical tilts, -2 to all sources of damage.<br /> Motus -&gt; Str+Athl+Azoth roll to get +Successes on non-combat Str and Stamina, longer jumps, +3 Str +3 Sta +1 Dext, rote on non-combat Str/Sta actions.Doubles speed (tripled with Zephyrus).<br /> <br /> Str -&gt; 23 (33 for breaking free)<br /> Dext -&gt; 22<br /> Sta -&gt; 23<br /> Res -&gt; 20<br /> Perception -&gt; 20 (30 to avoid surprise)<br /> Initiative -&gt; 42<br /> Health -&gt; 29<br /> Speed is at 150.<br /> Spending Pyros bumps actions up another +10.<br /> <br /> (Could add the Stalker Alembic for another +10 to Stealth.)<br /> Add Beastiae Facies to calculate with the higher of Dext and Wits - oh look, defense just went up to 27! Also, another +1 Str, +1 Size, +2 to Speed (if charged first, to base Speed), +1 to Perception.<br /> Plumb the Fathoms: +1 to resist social/mental supernatural powers, if passive resistance trait + Azoth<br /> Receptive Humour: +Azoth to Perception<br /> <br /> Str -&gt; 24 (34 for breaking free)<br /> Dext -&gt; 22<br /> Sta -&gt; 23<br /> Res -&gt; 20<br /> Perception -&gt; 31 (41 to avoid surprise)<br /> Initiative -&gt; 42<br /> Health -&gt; 30<br /> Speed -&gt; 156<br /> <br /> Not to mention all the rotes and 9-agains and &quot;exceptional success at 3&quot;.<br /> Respectable, imo.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: BTW, that Beast incarnate?<br /> 10 Base, 10 Titanic Onslaught, 10 for Cyclopean Strength, 11 for Skin Deep, 10 for Vengeful Earth SatExp. Limbs -&gt; 51 Strength (or as HelmsDerp detailed, up to 61 if taking Str rather than Titanic Onslaught.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 08-30-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-30T13:31:51-07:00","id":1250051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1250033#post1250033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: BTW, that Beast incarnate?<br /> 10 Base, 10 Titanic Onslaught, 10 for Cyclopean Strength, 11 for Skin Deep, 10 for Vengeful Earth SatExp. Limbs -&gt; 51 Strength (or as HelmsDerp detailed, up to 61 if taking Str rather than Titanic Onslaught.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Add in the Mage's boost and you could get 76/86, and slightly pass 100 with the KoSA mage double dipping thing. 101 STR if that 51 is real dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T05:38:12-07:00","id":1250716,"title":"","content":"I realized a few mistakes in my above calculations, and realized how to turn up the numbers: base 11 (epic potential), 20 str instead of Titanic onslaught, 11 For Skin Deep, 10 For Cyclopean Strength, and now the fun part: another 20 if in Horror Form and pumpen everything into power. +10 on the stone limbs created through vengeful earth: 63 dice on power rolls (equal to 63 Str/Int/Pres) with another +10 on successes and another +10 for using stone limbs -&gt; 83.<br /> Add in Limb from Limb, and a single success deals 21 L or 21 A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T00:11:01-07:00","id":1251855,"title":"","content":"While not an actual Attribute, a Beast Incarnate can hit Size 36 with the Satiety use of Looming Presence and Legendary Size for +(Lair*3) to size. Which, when used with Cyclopean Strength, means they can lift any object of <b>Size 396</b> or less. Then, with the Low Satiety use of Cyclopean Strength they can use it as an improvised weapon. I'm not sure of anything that large that could withstand the stress of that much for to actually be <i>used</i>, but still.<br /> <br /> This is also in addition to getting a Strength of 42+10 success to all Strength rolls (which can get another [Lair] dice to intiate a Grapple with Crushing Coils).<br /> <br /> In Dream Form they could hit Size 46 which would let them lift objects up to <b>Size 506</b>, and since it's a dream you could justify it actually holding together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T18:18:57-07:00","id":1252066,"title":"","content":"So, as a side question, how fast could each splat move? I'm talking about how high can we make someone's speed advantage, not teleportation, flying, or astral self. It has to be the physical body moving from point A to point B on a straight road, while needing to move on the entire road for the duration of the race.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T21:31:11-07:00","id":1252119,"title":"","content":"Beast complicates this because on an infinitely long road with people along it at a regular interval, a Beast could theoretically move infinitely in one turn (though statistically they wouldn't actually do it). There's a power that lets a Beast attack an opponent and if they deal damage (not hard to do with maxed out traits and all) they can attack another target within (Lair x 10 yard), and they can repeat until there's no target within range or no new targets to strike.<br /> <br /> So this fits in your existing criteria, but doesn't seem to fit the spirit of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T22:44:43-07:00","id":1252130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1252066#post1252066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as a side question, how fast could each splat move? I'm talking about how high can we make someone's speed advantage, not teleportation, flying, or astral self. It has to be the physical body moving from point A to point B on a straight road, while needing to move on the entire road for the duration of the race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to find the thread, and it's out of date now, but the last winner was a Sin-Eater merging with basically a god-machine that actually exists in real life and blows your god damned mind.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Damnit, I think it was on the old forums, which is depressing because that thread also had the most beautiful Promethean you had ever seen.<br /> <br /> It went insane as it ran, for the record, and that's the <i>least weird part of it</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-07-2018, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T22:53:15-07:00","id":1252133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HunterInTheNight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1252066#post1252066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as a side question, how fast could each splat move? I'm talking about how high can we make someone's speed advantage, not teleportation, flying, or astral self. It has to be the physical body moving from point A to point B on a straight road, while needing to move on the entire road for the duration of the race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do vehicles count? Armory has the jet, which can get a speed of 2200 (but is technically flying, so I guess that is cheating :V). Supercar from the same book has 301, sports car has 249 which technically passes the criteria. If not, it would be fun to see who can run faster than a speeding sportscar :P.<br /> <br /> Since speed= Strength + Dex +5 (5 can be changed for some supernaturals) if we are talking about foot races, going back to the above &quot;maximum stat&quot; discussion would help get the answer. Most speed boosters work as a multiplier, for example a Vampire's Celerity could potentially multiple it by 6 for 1 point of Vitae, so that optimized vampire up there could probably outrun a speeding car without mage help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T23:03:09-07:00","id":1252135,"title":"","content":"I know there's a werewolf ability to possess a vehicle, so however fast a vehicle can go. And I'm pretty sure there's similar abilities in other gamelines, like demon has one.<br /> <br /> In the simple question thread we came up with ~74.56 mph for a werewolf using passive or long-term abilities (not abilities that worked for one turn). It also discounts fetishes, sorceries and rites that are pretty open ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T23:51:32-07:00","id":1252136,"title":"","content":"For static speed that lasts at least a scene:<br /> Prometheans can reach speeds Of 156, As Detailed above.<br /> Beasts can reach 48, I think (68 For Incarnate). Looming Presence satiety expenditure (race base raised to 15), Skin deep satiety expenditure (+12), epic potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T03:15:19-07:00","id":1252158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1251855#post1251855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Dream Form they could hit Size 46 which would let them lift objects up to <b>Size 506</b>, and since it's a dream you could justify it actually holding together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember kids, don\u2019t piss off Atlas or he will <i>hit you with the sky</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 09-07-2018, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T03:45:45-07:00","id":1252164,"title":"","content":"I guess Vampires can reach a base speed of 48. That would be base stat 10+10 + 6 in size (giant) and +3 (fleet on foot) +5 from Vigor and +10 from Blood Potency via the Coil of Wyrm and +4 from running on all four with protean 2.<br /> With a multiplier of 6 with Celerity 5, this is 288 in base speed for one turn, (cost 1 vitae) and double if running.<br /> <br /> With the Devotion Forced March, she could run for hours with this speed, as long as she runs. Even though it's a 1st edition devotion, there's no reason to believe it wouldn't work in 2ed.<br /> <br /> That's a running speed of 576. That's about 690 km/h or about 430 mph if my math is right.<br /> <br /> Mages on the other hand, could probably go even faster.<br /> With Velocity Control, for every potency, you double the Speed.<br /> <br /> So a mage, maxed out from running as above would have a base of 29 if i'm correct. With a rote and such, she could easily have potency 10 on this spell, that's a base speed of 29696.<br /> With running that's 59392. That would be about 71 000 kilometers per hour. If you do some actual math with mages, I'm sure you could reach even more ludicrous speed if Colonel Sanders ain't a chicken.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T04:18:19-07:00","id":1252171,"title":"","content":"Species factor to Speed for humans is 5, I thought, not Size (so Giant doesn't give 6)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T04:32:50-07:00","id":1252174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1252171#post1252171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Species factor to Speed for humans is 5, I thought, not Size (so Giant doesn't give 6)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quick ref chart in vampire 2ed says its size, but other say species factor of 5. So yeah you're probably right. One less in base speed in my calcs then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T05:51:03-07:00","id":1252191,"title":"","content":"You can instead add +5 from Praestantia that pushes Dex up to 15.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T19:55:25-07:00","id":1252646,"title":"","content":"Would Acceleration, Ground Eater, and Velocity Control interact at all? Or would it just be what ever gives the biggest bonus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T20:18:24-07:00","id":1252650,"title":"","content":"Granted, it's a flight speed and it (on average) lasts less than a minute, but Beasts can take that 51 (you forgot fleet of foot's +3) and multiply it by 11 with Wings of the Raptor. Not as crazy as Mages but half the speed of sound ain't bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T02:28:46-07:00","id":1252703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1252646#post1252646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Acceleration, Ground Eater, and Velocity Control interact at all? Or would it just be what ever gives the biggest bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do things differently, so they should interact. Ground Eater is a straight boost of Potency to Speed, Acceleration multiplies it, and Velocity Control exponentially increases speed (not the Speed derived trait). Combine them in that order after Attribute boosts and...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T04:40:14-07:00","id":1252721,"title":"","content":"And you'll need to dedicate another spell to making sure you aren't vaporized by the air resistance as you go streaking along at a substantial fraction of the speed of light.<br /> <br /> Possibly more than one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T07:27:58-07:00","id":1252758,"title":"","content":"Might just be a single Forces Shielding spell. Iirc Shielding usually makes you outright immune to non-supernatural damage that doesn't come from attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-09T09:21:35-07:00","id":1252777,"title":"","content":"2E has largely done away with 'add extra spells/arcana to make your spell actually work as intended due to technicalities'<br /> <br /> IMO, you wouldn't need this any more than you'd need Mind to enhance your brain's abilities to perceive the world around it in order to successfully navigate at that high of a speed. That was very much a first edition thing. Same way you don't need Mind to let yourself interpret radio waves into useful data after you cast a spell to let you hear them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:59:09-07:00","id":1253177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1252703#post1252703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do things differently, so they should interact. Ground Eater is a straight boost of Potency to Speed, Acceleration multiplies it, and Velocity Control exponentially increases speed (not the Speed derived trait). Combine them in that order after Attribute boosts and...?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking. Which would make a speed of over 307 <b>thousand</b> completely doable. Which is really just silly when you think about it. Fun, but silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T20:38:26-07:00","id":1253205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1245867-maximum-achievable-attribute-score?p=1253177#post1253177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I was thinking. Which would make a speed of over 307 <b>thousand</b> completely doable. Which is really just silly when you think about it. Fun, but silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>But like he said, that is speed not Speed. At that point you are basically a projectile :V. Velocity Control doesn't let the object actually control itself at those speeds.<br /> <br /> Find a Peasant and you have yourself a unique, literal version of the peasant railgun! Bribe your ST with food and an incredibly loose reading of the rules that say it changes damaged based on collision to turn your minions into potent projectiles! Just be sure to stay out of the blast range and/or splash zone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}